> Derive Hebbian storage and the energy change

For P bipolar memories xi, normalized Hebbian storage sets

$$W_{ij}=\frac1N\sum_{p=1}^{P}\xi_i^{(p)}\xi_j^{(p)}\quad(i\ne j),\qquad W_{ii}=0.$$
\alttext(Each distinct-neuron weight sums pairwise products across memories and divides by the number of neurons; self-connections are zero.)

The canonical storage function adds the supplied products in pattern order, then
multiplies by the computed double reciprocal of N. This preserves the historical
arithmetic. All inputs must be rectangular and bipolar before multiplication,
preventing invalid integer products. Empty pattern dimensions produce an empty
network. This is direct Hebbian storage; the demonstrated rule is not an
optimizer fit to a classification loss.

For state s and symmetric zero-diagonal W, define h_i=sum_j W_ij*s_j and
E(s)=-1/2 sum_ij W_ij*s_i*s_j. If only neuron i changes to s'_i, symmetry makes
its two contributions combine:

$$E(s')-E(s)=-(s'_i-s_i)h_i.$$
\alttext(The energy difference from a single-neuron update equals minus its sign change times the previous local field.)

Choosing the field's sign makes this nonpositive in exact arithmetic. At exactly
zero field, this implementation chooses +1, including when the old sign is -1.
Such a flip leaves energy unchanged. The old documentation's assertion that ties
kept the current sign did not match its code; the actual positive-tie behavior
is preserved here.

In the exact finite-state model, strict field-driven flips decrease energy. A
zero-energy flip only changes -1 to+1, so it reduces the number of negative
signs while energy stays fixed. The lexicographic pair (energy, number of
negative signs) therefore decreases whenever a sign changes, which rules out
cycles in that exact model. Each full sweep visits every neuron, so eventually a
sweep is unchanged. Sequential floating fields and diagnostic energies are
rounded calculations; their errors can invalidate an exact sign or energy
certificate near cancellation. The finite sweep budget remains an explicit
bound, and the run distinguishes an observed unchanged sweep from a budget stop.

The initial network must have a square finite matrix, exact symmetry and zero
diagonal. States must have exactly N entries, all -1 or +1. The complete
model/state checks precede indexed use, preventing the old unchecked energy
access on short states. Nonfinite producing sums throw. Hamming distance
likewise requires complete equal-length bipolar states, rather than silently
discarding a longer suffix.

> Retain the original hundred-neuron experiment

Use the original data seed 20240730, three Bernoulli bipolar memories of length
100 and three additional random comparison states. The experiment draws the
noisy probe by toggling ten uniform positions with replacement. In this current
execution those ten draws change only six positions; toggling a position twice
cancels it. The legacy cached result said ten changed bits, so it cannot
substitute for the executed program.

The matrix and recall retain the original algorithm, RNG draw order and seeds.
Standard-library distribution and shuffle mappings can differ between
implementations, even with the same engine seed. The retained complete probes
and outputs, and the local frozen comparisons, make the current results
checkable. Lower energy than three random states alone would not establish
stored-pattern stability; the table separately checks whether one whole recall
sweep changes each memory.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopfield_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto e = dm::algorithms::hopfield_original_experiment();
    std::print("| memory | stored-state energy | comparison-state energy | flips in one stored-state sweep " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < e.memories.size(); ++i) {
        const auto fixed =
            dm::algorithms::hopfield_recall_run(e.network, e.memories[i], 1, 7);
        std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {} |\n", i,
                   dm::algorithms::hopfield_energy(e.network, e.memories[i]),
                   dm::algorithms::hopfield_energy(e.network, e.random_states[i]),
                   fixed.work.flips);
    }
    const auto &t = e.probe_trace;
    std::print("\nTen sampled toggles; actual initial Hamming {}; final Hamming {}; producing field terms " "{}; neuron decisions {}; flips {}; separate diagnostic-energy terms {}.\n",
               dm::algorithms::hopfield_hamming(e.probe, e.memories[0]),
               dm::algorithms::hopfield_hamming(t.run.state, e.memories[0]),
               t.run.work.field_terms, t.run.work.neuron_updates,
               t.run.work.flips, t.run.work.diagnostic_energy_terms);
    std::print("\n| actual sweep | flips | observed energy before | observed energy after |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<double> x{0.}, energy{t.initial_energy};
    for (const auto &sweep : t.sweeps) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n", sweep.sweep, sweep.flips,
                   sweep.energy_before, sweep.energy_after);
        x.push_back(sweep.sweep);
        energy.push_back(sweep.energy_after);
    }
    auto strip =
        dm::algorithms::hopfield_states_plot({e.memories[0], e.probe,
                                              t.run.state},
                                             "Top to bottom: target memory / actual probe / recall");
    auto curve = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    curve.line(x, energy, "actual energies", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).points(
        x, energy, "", {37, 99, 235}, 5.).title("Actual producing recall: sweep-boundary observations").x_label("complete sweeps, zero is initialization").y_label("computed energy").y_limits(*std::min_element(energy.begin(), energy.end()) - 5, *std::max_element(energy.begin(), energy.end()) + 15);
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1);
    layout.add(strip).add(curve).size(1100, 900).title("Original 100-neuron fixture: actual state and energy").fit_panels().save_svg("build/hopfield_original.svg");
    if (dm::algorithms::hopfield_hamming(t.run.state, e.memories[0]) != 0)
        throw std::runtime_error("original recall");
}
