> Bit agreement is not exact pattern recovery

Preserve the original eleven noise levels 0,5,..50 and thirty trials per level.
Every position is tested independently against its nominal flip percentage, so
actual Hamming distance varies. Each level creates fresh probes of memory 0;
recall seeds 1..30 repeat at every level. These are 330 finite trials on one
stored pattern in one generated network, not a population capacity or
generalization benchmark.

The old metric was mean fraction of correct output bits. A trial with one
hundred-neuron output error contributes 0.99 to bit agreement but zero to exact
whole-pattern recovery. The native experiment retains every actual input/output
state and reports both measures, the mean input distance and the actual number
of unchanged-sweep stops. An unchanged state can still be the wrong memory or an
unstored attractor.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopfield_noise.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto e = dm::algorithms::hopfield_original_experiment();
    std::print("| nominal flip percent | trials | mean actual input Hamming | exact recovered | no-change " "stops | mean output bit agreement | exact recovery fraction |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<double> x, bits, exact;
    for (const auto &s : e.summaries) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.6f} | {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
                   s.noise_percent, s.trials, s.mean_initial_distance,
                   s.exact_recoveries, s.no_change_stops, s.bit_agreement,
                   s.exact_recovery_fraction);
        x.push_back(s.noise_percent);
        bits.push_back(s.bit_agreement);
        exact.push_back(s.exact_recovery_fraction);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, bits, "bit agreement", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).points(x, bits, "",
                                                               {37, 99, 235}, 4.).line(x, exact, "exact patterns", {220, 38, 38}, 2.).points(x, exact, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4.).title("Original 330 trials: two different recovery summaries").x_label("nominal independent flip percent").y_label("observed fraction").y_limits(-.05, 1.3).save_svg("build/hopfield_noise.svg");
    if (e.trials.size() != 330 || e.summaries.size() != 11)
        throw std::runtime_error("complete experiment");
}
