> Work, bounded histories and invalid inputs

Storage takes O(P*N*N+P*N+1) work and O(N*N+1) output. Ordinary recall first
validates the complete matrix/state, then uses O(N*N+S*N*N+S*N+1) work and
O(N+1) additional working/output storage beyond the borrowed weights, for S
complete sweeps. Its producing counters record every field term, neuron decision
and actual sign flip; they exclude validation, copies, RNG/shuffle and
allocation. The trace separately counts its extra initial/end-sweep full-energy
terms: (S+1)N^2 for these examples. These diagnostics add work and can overflow
even if the untraced fields would remain finite.

New checked storage/run/trace calls default to 10000 neurons and one million
weight entries, including diagonal, with zero disabling either policy. Full
domain checks precede these caps and internal copies. Legacy interfaces retain
no optional matrix cap. Initial trace admission is 1+N logical units, then 1+3N
per known whole sweep: a sweep record, N order IDs, N state values and N update
records. Scalar record fields, metadata, capacity, ordinary working/output
storage and byte/peak-memory use are outside this one-million-unit policy.
Admission precedes shuffle/copies and throws instead of returning truncated
history; untraced execution ignores the history cap.

The complete study also admits all 11*T trials before generation or training,
defaulting to a 10000-trial cap. Native state views validate every sign and row
before a separate complete display-cell cap. These limits have different units
and are not interchangeable memory budgets.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopfield_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto net = dm::algorithms::hopfield_train({{-1}});
    const auto exact =
        dm::algorithms::hopfield_recall_trace(net, {-1}, 1, 0, {1, 1, 6});
    bool history =
        false, matrix = false, domain = false, length = false, study = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopfield_recall_trace(net, {-1}, 1, 0, {1, 1, 5});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        history = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopfield_train_checked({{1, -1}}, {2, 3, 0});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        matrix = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopfield_recall_run(dm::algorithms::HopfieldNetwork{{{0, 1}, {2, 0}}},
                                                   {1, 1}, 1, 0, {1, 1, 1});
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        domain = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopfield_hamming({1}, {1, -1});
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        length = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopfield_original_experiment(30, 20240730, 329);
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        study = true;
    }
    std::print("Exact one-neuron/one-sweep capture {}; one-short history rejected {}; one-short complete " "weight cap rejected {}; malformed matrix beats exceeded policy {}; unequal Hamming lengths " "rejected {}; one-short complete study rejected {}.\n",
               exact.captured_entries, history, matrix, domain, length, study);
    std::vector<double> x, field, diagnostic;
    std::print("\n| neurons | actual sweeps | field terms | separate energy terms | capture units |\n| ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {2, 4, 8, 16, 32}) {
        const std::vector<int> memory(n, 1);
        const auto model = dm::algorithms::hopfield_train_checked({memory});
        auto probe = memory;
        probe[0] = -1;
        const auto t =
            dm::algorithms::hopfield_recall_trace(model, probe, 10, 0);
        x.push_back(n);
        field.push_back(t.run.work.field_terms);
        diagnostic.push_back(t.run.work.diagnostic_energy_terms);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, t.run.sweeps,
                   t.run.work.field_terms, t.run.work.diagnostic_energy_terms,
                   t.captured_entries);
        if (t.run.work.field_terms != n * n * t.run.sweeps ||
            t.run.work.diagnostic_energy_terms != n * n * (t.run.sweeps + 1))
            throw std::runtime_error("actual work");
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, field, "field terms", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(
        x, diagnostic, "extra energy terms", {220, 38, 38}, 2.).title(
        "Actual producing work and extra trace diagnostics").x_label("neurons").y_label("selected weighted-state terms").y_limits(0, 4500).save_svg("build/hopfield_limits.svg");
    if (!history || !matrix || !domain || !length || !study)
        throw std::runtime_error("complete policies");
}
```
