\caption(Counts use actual completed sweeps for each size. Extra energy observations are separated from producing local-field work and are never labelled as free tracing.)
\alttext(Two curves compare actual local-field terms with additional full-energy diagnostic terms across several small neuron counts.)

> Verification and primary source

Native sanitizer tests reconstruct actual fields, signs, permutations, energies
and work across all 255 nonempty subsets of the three-neuron pattern space,
every starting state and two shuffle seeds. They also cover the correlated/tie
cases, zero budgets/dimensions, malformed/nonfinite/overflowing matrices,
sign/shape/complete-policy failures, ownership, complete-study limits and actual
fixed-palette display orientation. Frozen valid-input comparisons preserve 12240
recalls, 255 matrices and 2040 energies exactly. A separate frozen check
preserves the complete original draw stream, probe, all 330 trial outputs and
all 11 bit-agreement summaries. An independent Fraction oracle checks 4084
producing histories, 23040 update decisions and 11701 energy observations using
the exact dyadic values of the stored double weights. Existing Hopfield/SOM/RBF
tests, compiled documentation examples, representative hovers, actual MEP
executions, inspected native figures and byte-checked Markdown/HTML result/image
exports are conversion gates. No arbitrary cached numerical result replaces a
current execution.

The foundational source is [J. J. Hopfield, Neural networks and physical systems
with emergent collective computational
abilities](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC346238/), PNAS 79(8),
2554–2558, 1982, [DOI
10.1073/pnas.79.8.2554](https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.79.8.2554). This report
uses the library's normalized bipolar, zero-threshold, shuffled-sweep and
positive-zero-tie conventions. Its finite generated experiment supports the
reported outcomes, not a universal nearest-memory or capacity guarantee.
